diagnosis_text:
There is no fault in this network. The helpdesk ticket and the team's
interpretation are both incorrect. Direct probing of the live dc_clos_bgp lab
shows the following: (1) An ICMP ping from pc_0_0 (10.0.0.2) to pc_0_1
(10.0.1.2) completes with 0% packet loss and sub-2 ms latency across all four
probes, proving end-to-end reachability is fully intact. (2) Both uplink
interfaces on leaf_router_0_1 — eth0 (toward spine_router_0_0) and eth1 (toward
spine_router_0_1) — report state UP with LOWER_UP carrier, meaning the physical
and data-link layers are operational on both links. The spine-side counterpart
interfaces (spine_router_0_0:eth2 and spine_router_0_1:eth2) are equally UP with
carrier. (3) Both BGP sessions on leaf_router_0_1 are in Established state with
prefixes received from each spine (AS 65100 and AS 65101, up-time ~1m45s), and
leaf_router_0_0's sessions are also fully established. The control plane is
converged and the data plane carries traffic normally. The root cause of the
ticket is a false premise: no uplink failure occurred, no BGP session dropped,
and no user traffic is actually being dropped. No corrective action is required
on any device or link; the team should close the ticket and verify their
monitoring source, which may have reported a stale or spurious alarm.
=== END ===
